śarīra-stho ’pi kaunteya
na karoti na lipyate\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":3799,\"bb\":3345,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/13/32/b3345/\",\"shadow_value\":\"anāditvāt – due to eternity; nirguṇatvāt – due to being transcendental; parama – beyond material nature; ātmā – spirit; ayam – this; avyayaḥ – inexhaustible; śarīra-sthaḥ – dwelling in the body; api – though; kaunteya – O son of Kuntī; na karoti – never does anything; na lipyate – nor is he entangled.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"anāditvāt\",\"translation\":\"due to eternity\"},{\"word\":\"nirguṇatvāt\",\"translation\":\"due to being transcendental\"},{\"word\":\"parama\",\"translation\":\"beyond material nature\"},{\"word\":\"ātmā\",\"translation\":\"spirit\"},{\"word\":\"ayam\",\"translation\":\"this\"},{\"word\":\"avyayaḥ\",\"translation\":\"inexhaustible\"},{\"word\":\"śarīra-sthaḥ\",\"translation\":\"dwelling in the body\"},{\"word\":\"api\",\"translation\":\"though\"},{\"word\":\"kaunteya\",\"translation\":\"O son of Kuntī\"},{\"word\":\"na karoti\",\"translation\":\"never does anything\"},{\"word\":\"na lipyate\",\"translation\":\"nor is he entangled\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":3800,\"bb\":3346,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/13/32/b3346/\",\"body_value\":\"Those with the vision of eternity can see that the imperishable soul is transcendental, eternal, and beyond the modes of nature. Despite contact with the material body, O Arjuna, the soul neither does anything nor is entangled.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":3801,\"bb\":3347,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/13/32/b3347/\",\"body_value\":\"A living entity appears to be born because of the birth of the material body, b